<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Qualitative Comparisons with State-of-the-Art Methods</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present extended qualitative comparisons with state-of-the-art (SOTA) methods in Fig. <a href="#A2.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix B Additional Qualitative Comparisons with State-of-the-Art Methods ‣ Lego-Edit: A General Image Editing Framework with Model-Level Bricks and MLLM Builder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. The comparison methods include InstructP2P <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brooks et al. (2023)</a></cite>, ComfyMind <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al. (2025)</a></cite>, BAGEL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al. (2025)</a></cite>, OmniGen2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, Step-1X <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, Uniworld-V1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12883v1/a1.png" id="A2.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/163;" width="548" height="163" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Qualitative comparison with state-of-the-art methods.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Further examples demonstrating performance across different aspect ratios are shown in Fig. <a href="#A2.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ Appendix B Additional Qualitative Comparisons with State-of-the-Art Methods ‣ Lego-Edit: A General Image Editing Framework with Model-Level Bricks and MLLM Builder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Fig. <a href="#A2.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Appendix B Additional Qualitative Comparisons with State-of-the-Art Methods ‣ Lego-Edit: A General Image Editing Framework with Model-Level Bricks and MLLM Builder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> showcases results achieved with more complex and flexible instructions.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12883v1/a3.png" id="A2.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/316;" width="548" height="316" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Qualitative results of handling complex and flexible editing instructions.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F13" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12883v1/a2.png" id="A2.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:439/728;" width="439" height="728" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>Qualitative results for image editing at varying aspect ratios.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Qualitative Analysis of Task Confusion in Joint Training</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As discussed in the main paper, joint training approaches such as ICEdit <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025)</a></cite> can suffer from task confusion. While quantitative evidence is presented therein, Fig. <a href="#A3.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ Appendix C Qualitative Analysis of Task Confusion in Joint Training ‣ Lego-Edit: A General Image Editing Framework with Model-Level Bricks and MLLM Builder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> provides qualitative examples illustrating this phenomenon.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F14" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12883v1/a5.png" id="A3.F14.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:329/283;" width="329" height="283" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span>Qualitative examples of task confusion arising from joint model training.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F15" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12883v1/a4.png" id="A3.F15.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:329/217;" width="329" height="217" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span>Qualitative improvements achieved through strategic composition of model-level tools.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Qualitative Benefits of Tool Composition</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The main paper presents quantitative results demonstrating the performance gains achieved by composing specific tools (e.g., RES for color/style change, CAP-PRED for style change). Fig. <a href="#A3.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ Appendix C Qualitative Analysis of Task Confusion in Joint Training ‣ Lego-Edit: A General Image Editing Framework with Model-Level Bricks and MLLM Builder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> offers corresponding qualitative evidence of these improvements.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Complete Prompt Template for the Builder Agent</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The full prompt used to configure the Builder agent is provided in Listing <a href="#LST1" title="Listing 1 ‣ Appendix E Complete Prompt Template for the Builder Agent ‣ Lego-Edit: A General Image Editing Framework with Model-Level Bricks and MLLM Builder" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
